.TH EDEX-UI-TUI 1 "October 2026" "eDEX-UI TUI alpha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
edex-ui-tui \- terminal workspace inspired by eDEX-UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B edex-ui-tui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a dedicated Kitty window with native tmux shells, Linux instruments
and a file browser. The on-screen keyboard starts hidden.
Run from a graphical Linux desktop with at least 140 columns by 40 rows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
List launcher and session options.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " directory"
Choose the initial working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-skip-intro
Skip the startup sequence.
.TP
.BI \-\-files " auto|yazi|superfile|preview"
Choose file navigation. The icon grid needs Yazi 26.9.1 or newer and librsvg.
.TP
.B \-\-toggle-keyboard
Show or hide the keyboard in the existing project session.
.TP
.B \-\-install-shell-frame
Enable the experimental clipped shell frame in the existing session.
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Stop the project session, including its native shells. Finish shell work first.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B EDEX_TMUX_SOCKET
selects a separate project tmux server. Use the same value for launch and controls.
.SH LIMITS
This alpha targets one local Kitty client with temporary-file graphics.
Kitty and Python must share a filesystem. Existing workers retain their loaded
code after a package upgrade; stop and relaunch after finishing shell work.
Remote graphics, mobile input and popup movement remain validation work.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/doc/edex-ui-tui
contains usage, provenance, licenses and validation notes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kitty (1),
.BR tmux (1)
